<title>RUSSIA: Gas blast kills four miners in Russian Far East.</title>
<headline>Gas blast kills four miners in Russian Far East.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Four coal miners died and another was wounded in a methane gas explosion on the island of Sakhalin in the Russian Far East, a spokesman for the Emergencies Ministry said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The blast in the Sakhalinugol coal mine occurred  early on Thursday after a gas leak, the spokesman said.</p>
<p>An investigation is under way.</p>
